# L §6.4, §8.3 item 9 (tally 2.1.6, P29 on T's SR-T1 of #75): a binding's `where` that reads nothing but the keys is
# seen at load, which folds it at every key: top keeps the first day of each month, 2026-01-01 alone in the run, on or
# after D, so topup loads and answers. 2.1.6's first refcore (522a715) folded the day at every key of days, the where
# unread, and refused topup, LOAD-SCENARIO top books on 2025-12-30. Twin: _where_keys_refused.
=== base.tally
model hh
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-02
  start 2025-12-30
  end 2026-01-05

source s "s"

unit PLN: currency minor 0.01

place konto: accounts PLN lives 2025-01-01..

place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..

input from_day: date

input early: date

ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-05)

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  from_day = 2026-01-01
  early = 2025-01-01
  opening[konto] = 10.00 PLN at 2025-12-30 start
=== scen.tally
scenario topup over hh
  tally 2
  from 2026-01-01

move top[d in days where d == start_of(month_of(d))]: transfers
  on d
  leg cash from world to konto amount 1.00 PLN

ask q_top: bal(konto, 2026-01-05) in topup
=== expect q_top
q_top: 11.00 PLN
  world: topup
  unfulfilled: top[2026-01-01]
  cut 2026-01-02
warning: WARN-UNREAD input early is read by nothing
warning: WARN-UNREAD input from_day is read by nothing
